@startuml
!include _libcpg-theme.iuml
title DfgExtractor::visit_reaching — AST-ordered reaching-definitions sweep
start
:initialize ReachingEnv = empty
a map from name to its reaching definitions,
binding parameters before the function body;<<#FFF3BF>>
repeat
:visit next AST node in source (AST child) order;<<#DBE4FF>>
if (node is a definition?) then (yes)
  if (enclosing context?) then (straight-line)
    :strong update (kill + gen) in straight-line context;<<#FFF3BF>>
  else (conditional region)
    :weak update (add, no kill);<<#FFF3BF>>
  endif
else (no)
endif
if (node is a use?) then (yes)
  :link use to current ReachingEnv definitions
(incl. nested-expression uses);<<#FFF3BF>>
else (no)
endif
if (node is a loop region: While / For / Loop?) then (yes)
  :sweep loop body twice for loop-carried deps;<<#FFF3BF>>
else (no)
endif
repeat while (more AST nodes in source order?) is (yes) not (no)
stop

note right
  Idempotent, flow-sensitive sweep.
  <b>NOT SSA</b> — no phi nodes.
  <b>NOT CFG-propagated</b> — reaching
  definitions flow along AST child
  order, threaded down into the
  nested-expression uses of each
  statement (e.g. x in return f(x)).
end note

legend right
  |= colour |= sweep step |
  |<#DBE4FF>| AST traversal (visit node) |
  |<#FFF3BF>| DataFlow — reaching-definition update / use link |
endlegend
@enduml
